                        <field name="dc_description">Published in Cork, by John Bolster, Patrick-Street sold, also, by all booksellers in Great Britain and Ireland. -- Price: sixpence. -- Entered at Stationers'-Hall. At foot of title: "With an appendix containing two letters on the union of the two churches (first published in the year 1824), one by Dr. Doyle, late R.C. Bishop of Kildare, the other by the author himself". -- Inscription on t.p.: "This copy is respectfully present to Colonel [?] William Gossett by the author". -- Appendix includes letter from Right Rev. Dr. Doyle to A. Robertson, Esq., M.P., dated "Carlow,May 13th, 1824"  and letter from the author to the editor of the Cork Mercantile Chronicle, dated "Courceys, June, 1824". -- Includes postscript. </field>
